4. What was the biggest production issue you faced?

This is very likely in a managerial round.

A strong answer:

> We once faced a production issue where an API was taking significantly longer than expected.

I first checked the application logs and monitoring dashboards to identify whether the issue was related to application processing, database calls or an external dependency.

From the logs and metrics, we identified that the delay was coming from a database operation.

I analyzed the query and execution plan and identified the bottleneck. We optimized the query and also reviewed the indexing/pagination approach.

After deployment, we monitored the API response time and confirmed that the performance had improved.

We also documented the RCA and the preventive actions so that the issue wouldn't recur.



Managerial follow-up:
"How did you communicate this to the client?"

> I communicated the impact, current status, immediate mitigation and expected resolution clearly, without using unnecessary technical terminology. After fixing it, I shared the RCA and preventive measures.




